      "problem": "Solve for $u$, where $\\dfrac{u+2}{3} = - \\dfrac{3-u}{2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We transfer the negative into the numerator of the fraction, and proceed with cross-multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{u+2}{3} & =-\\frac{3-u}{2} \\\\ \\frac{u+2}{3} & =\\frac{-(3-u)}{2} \\\\ \\frac{u+2}{3} & =\\frac{-3+u}{2} \\\\ (u+2)\\cdot 2 & =3\\cdot (-3+u)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we proceed as usual to solve the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u+2)\\cdot 2 & =3\\cdot (-3+u) \\\\ 2u+4 & =-9+3u \\\\ 2u+4-2u & =-9+3u-2u \\\\ 4 & =-9+u \\\\ 4+9 & =-9+u+9 \\\\ 13 & =u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $u=13.$",
